---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout title="Notifications — Nexus Wave Technologies" description="Nexus notifications for important updates and private support follow-up.">
  <section class="hero"><div class="container hero-shell">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">Nexus Notifications</p><h1>Important updates, in one place.</h1><p class="lead">Notifications can keep you informed about support responses, case status changes, app updates and other important activity.</p></div>
    <div class="hero-panel"><p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p><h2>Support notifications reveal only the minimum necessary information.</h2><p class="muted">Private case details stay inside the protected support flow.</p></div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="container grid-3">
    <article class="card"><p class="eyebrow">Support</p><h3>Case response</h3><p class="muted">A future notification can tell you that a support worker has replied or become available.</p></article>
    <article class="card"><p class="eyebrow">Security</p><h3>Account alerts</h3><p class="muted">Important authentication or privacy events can be surfaced here without exposing sensitive data.</p></article>
    <article class="card"><p class="eyebrow">Nexus</p><h3>Product updates</h3><p class="muted">Relevant app and service announcements can appear here.</p></article>
  </div></section>
  <section class="section surface-soft"><div class="container">
    <div class="section-card">
      <h2>Notifications are ready for the app workflow.</h2>
      <p class="muted">The public website currently provides the information architecture. Authenticated app users can later receive the same notification contract through Supabase Realtime and push notifications.</p>
      <a class="button primary" href="/apps">Explore Nexus Apps</a>
    </div>
  </div></section>
</Layout>